-- title:
--   Theorem 7.3 — the push-up-then-push-down prices converge to a stationary point of the expected revenue
-- statement:
--   Consider the $d$-level nested logit price model under its standing assumptions ($\beta_l>0$ for every product, $\eta_j\in(0,1]$ for every nonleaf node $j\neq\mathrm{root}$, $\eta_{\mathrm{root}}=0$), with expected revenue $R_{\mathrm{root}}(\mathbf p)$. Let $\mathbf p^0=\mathbf 0,\mathbf p^1,\mathbf p^2,\dots$ be the price vectors of the push-up-then-push-down algorithm: $p^{s+1}_l=1/\beta_l+t^s_{\mathrm{Parent}(l)}$, where $t^s_{\mathrm{root}}=R_{\mathrm{root}}(\mathbf p^s)$ and $t^s_j=\max\{t^s_{\mathrm{Parent}(j)},\ \eta_jt^s_{\mathrm{Parent}(j)}+(1-\eta_j)R_j(\mathbf p^s)\}$.
--
--   Then the sequence converges, and its limit is a stationary point of $R_{\mathrm{root}}$: there is $\mathbf p^*\in\mathbb R^n$ with
--   $$
--   \lim_{s\to\infty}\mathbf p^s=\mathbf p^*\qquad\text{and}\qquad \nabla R_{\mathrm{root}}(\mathbf p^*)=0 .
--   $$
--
--   Since $R_{\mathrm{root}}$ is in general not concave, a stationary point is the natural target; the theorem says the gradient-free PUPD iteration reaches one without a step size.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Convergence is of the whole sequence (`Filter.Tendsto` along `atTop`), not of a subsequence, and stationarity is `HasFDerivAt R_root 0 p*`, as in Corollary 7.2. The start point is fixed at $\mathbf p^0=\mathbf 0$ as in Step 0 of the algorithm.
-- source:
--   Li, Rusmevichientong, Topaloglu, The d-Level Nested Logit Model: Assortment and Price Optimization Problems, Oper. Res. 63(2), 2015, p. 336, Theorem 7.3

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_DLevelNestedLogit_Pricing_PUPD

namespace DLevelNestedLogit.Pricing

/-- Theorem 7.3 (Li, Rusmevichientong, Topaloglu 2015, p. 336): the sequence of prices
`p^0 = 0, p^1, p^2, …` generated by the push-up-then-push-down algorithm converges, and its
limit is a stationary point of the expected revenue function `R_root` (the gradient of
`R_root` at the limit is zero). -/
theorem pupd_converges_stationary {n d : ℕ} (T : DLevelTree n d) (P : Params T)
    (hP : P.Standing) :
    ∃ pstar : Fin n → ℝ, Filter.Tendsto (pupd P) Filter.atTop (nhds pstar) ∧
      HasFDerivAt (expectedRevenue P) (0 : (Fin n → ℝ) →L[ℝ] ℝ) pstar := by sorry

end DLevelNestedLogit.Pricing
